  "preview": "A hot air balloon starts at 1,200 m and descends at 3/4 m per second. When does it land below safety altitude? The negative rate flips the inequality.",
  "body": {
    "goal": "Solve a two-step inequality with a negative rational coefficient in context, with explicit attention to the inequality flip when dividing by a negative number, and interpret the boundary moment in the story.",
    "studentPrompt": "A hot air balloon takes off at 1,200 meters above the ground. The pilot opens a vent and the balloon begins to drift downward at a steady rate of 3/4 meter every second.\n\nThe pilot's safety chart says the balloon must stay above 450 meters until the landing crew radios that the field is clear.\n\nLet t be the number of seconds since the descent started.\n\n1. Write an expression for the balloon's altitude in terms of t.\n2. Write an inequality that represents the balloon being at or above the safety altitude of 450 m. Then solve it. For how many seconds can the balloon descend before it crosses the safety line?\n3. The landing crew radios 'all clear' after 15 minutes. Is the balloon still above the safety altitude? By how much, or below by how much?\n4. The pilot can speed up the descent by opening the vent wider — to 1.25 m/s. Rewrite the inequality with the new rate. How many MORE seconds does she lose before crossing the safety line, compared to the original rate?\n5. A second balloon takes off at 900 m and descends at 0.5 m/s. Which balloon crosses the 450 m safety line first?",
    "image": {
      "alt": "A red and orange hot air balloon high in a pale sky with an arrow pointing downward showing a descent rate, and a dashed safety altitude line below it.",
      "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 220\" font-family=\"system-ui, sans-serif\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"sky2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#cfe6f2\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#f6e9c8\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"480\" height=\"200\" fill=\"url(#sky2)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"480\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#a3c585\"/><circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"40\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#fff3b0\" opacity=\"0.8\"/><g opacity=\"0.7\" fill=\"#ffffff\"><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"7\"/><ellipse cx=\"75\" cy=\"45\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"6\"/><ellipse cx=\"410\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"7\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(180,30)\"><path d=\"M40,0 Q80,0 80,40 Q80,75 60,90 Q40,110 40,110 Q40,110 20,90 Q0,75 0,40 Q0,0 40,0 Z\" fill=\"#d94f4f\"/><path d=\"M40,0 Q60,0 65,40 Q70,75 55,90 L40,110 Q40,80 40,40 Q40,15 40,0 Z\" fill=\"#e88a3a\"/><path d=\"M40,0 Q20,0 15,40 Q10,75 25,90 L40,110 Q40,80 40,40 Q40,15 40,0 Z\" fill=\"#f2c54a\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#5a3a1e\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#5a3a1e\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"125\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a4a1e\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(280,90)\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#1f2a44\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><polygon points=\"-5,40 5,40 0,50\" fill=\"#1f2a44\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1f2a44\">3/4 m/s</text></g><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"460\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#b03a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#b03a3a\">Safety: 450 m</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1f2a44\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Start: 1,200 m</text></svg>"
    },
    "launch": "Show the image and tell the story. Ask: 'What does it mean to descend at three-quarters of a meter per second? Is that fast?' Then send them to boards. Do NOT pre-write the inequality.",
    "materials": [
      "Vertical whiteboards",
      "Markers",
      "Calculator allowed"
    ],
